<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alodia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 500–c. 1500</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a> · Also known as Alwa, Kingdom of Alodia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alodia, or Alwa, was the southernmost of the medieval Christian kingdoms of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nubia">Nubia</a>, centred on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-sudan">central Sudan</a> with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soba">Soba</a>, near the confluence of the Blue and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/white-nile">White Niles</a>. Converted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a> in the sixth century, it was described by Arab writers as larger and richer than Makuria. It declined in the late <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a>, and Soba fell to the Funj and the Abdallab around 1504.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alodia.jpg" alt="Alodia" width="320" height="238" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dekodrak · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Possible_Flag_of_the_Kingdom_of_Alodia_(c._1350).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
